        "id": "p133-q74-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $g(x)=\\dfrac{f(x)+f(-x)}{2}$ is even.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p133-q74-a-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "g",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " is even.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p133-q74-a-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "g(-x)=\\dfrac{f(-x)+f(x)}{2}=g(x)",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " for every real ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "x",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "For every $x\\in\\mathbb{R}$, both $x$ and $-x$ are in the domain.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}g(-x)&=\\frac{f(-x)+f(-(-x))}{2}\\\\g(-x)&=\\frac{f(-x)+f(x)}{2}\\\\g(-x)&=g(x).\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore $g$ is even.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p133-q74-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Show that $h(x)=\\dfrac{f(x)-f(-x)}{2}$ is odd.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p133-q74-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "h",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " is odd.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p133-q74-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "h(-x)=\\dfrac{f(-x)-f(x)}{2}=-h(x)",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " for every real ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "x",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}h(-x)&=\\frac{f(-x)-f(-(-x))}{2}\\\\h(-x)&=\\frac{f(-x)-f(x)}{2}\\\\h(-x)&=-\\frac{f(x)-f(-x)}{2}\\\\h(-x)&=-h(x).\\end{align*}$$\n\nThis holds for every $x\\in\\mathbb{R}$, so $h$ is odd.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p133-q74-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Hence, show that any function $f$ can be written as the sum of an even function and an odd function.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p133-q74-c-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "f(x)=g(x)+h(x)",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " on ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\mathbb{R}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", where ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "g",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " is even and ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "h",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " is odd.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p133-q74-c-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the half-sum and half-difference: the ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "f(-x)",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " terms cancel.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}g(x)+h(x)&=\\frac{f(x)+f(-x)}{2}+\\frac{f(x)-f(-x)}{2}\\\\g(x)+h(x)&=\\frac{f(x)+f(-x)+f(x)-f(-x)}{2}\\\\g(x)+h(x)&=\\frac{2f(x)}{2}\\\\g(x)+h(x)&=f(x).\\end{align*}$$\n\nBy (a) and (b), $g$ is even and $h$ is odd. Hence every function $f$ with domain $\\mathbb{R}$ can be written as $f(x)=g(x)+h(x)$, the sum of an even function and an odd function.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p133-q74-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Express $f(x)=2^x+3^{-2x}$ as the sum of an even and odd function.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p133-q74-d-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "f(x)=g(x)+h(x)",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", where",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "break"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "g(x)=\\dfrac{2^x+2^{-x}+3^{-2x}+3^{2x}}{2}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " is even,",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "break"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "h(x)=\\dfrac{2^x-2^{-x}+3^{-2x}-3^{2x}}{2}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " is odd.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p133-q74-d-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use the half-sum and half-difference with ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "f(-x)=2^{-x}+3^{2x}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=2^{-x}+3^{-2(-x)}\\\\f(-x)&=2^{-x}+3^{2x}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nForm the half-sum and half-difference:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}g(x)&=\\frac{f(x)+f(-x)}{2}\\\\g(x)&=\\frac{2^x+2^{-x}+3^{-2x}+3^{2x}}{2},\\\\h(x)&=\\frac{f(x)-f(-x)}{2}\\\\h(x)&=\\frac{2^x-2^{-x}+3^{-2x}-3^{2x}}{2}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nBy (a) and (b), $g$ is even and $h$ is odd on $\\mathbb{R}$. By (c),\n\n$$f(x)=g(x)+h(x).$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 72
      }
    ]
